Files derived from that work, and what changed:

  mamba3_pallas/torch_ref.py
      Copyright (c) 2026, Dao AI Lab, Goombalab
          (mamba_ssm/modules/mamba3.py, the Mamba3 module)
      Copyright (c) 2025, Dao AI Lab, Goombalab
          (tests/ops/triton/test_mamba3_siso.py, mamba3_siso_step_ref)

      Transcribed from those two files. Vendored instead of imported because
      mamba_ssm needs triton, tilelang and CUDA at import time, none of which
      exist on a TPU host. MIMO and varlen paths were removed. Upstream's two
      statement `A` clamp is kept as two statements on purpose, since folding
      it into one would reassociate the negation and flip the sign.

  mamba3_pallas/convert.py
      Copyright (c) 2026, Dao AI Lab, Goombalab
          (in_proj layout and state_dict key names from
           mamba_ssm/modules/mamba3.py)

      Depends on upstream's in_proj layout and state_dict key names so real
      checkpoints load. Adds the interleaved -> half-split rotary permutation,
      which upstream does not need.

  mamba3_pallas/reference.py
      Copyright (c) 2025, Dao AI Lab, Goombalab
          (recurrence structure from
           mamba_ssm/ops/triton/mamba3/mamba3_siso_fwd.py and
           mamba3_siso_combined.py)

      The recurrence equations follow the Mamba-3 paper and upstream's Triton
      kernel. The chunked form and the collapsed single-term scan are written
      from scratch here.

Everything else in mamba3_pallas/ is original work: the Pallas TPU kernels
(forward, backward, decode), the layout/BlockSpec machinery, the test suite
and the training code.

The algorithm is from:

  Mamba-3: Improved Sequence Modeling using State Space Principles.
  Aakash Lahoti, Kevin Y. Li, Berlin Chen, Caitlin Wang, Aviv Bick,
  J. Zico Kolter, Tri Dao, Albert Gu. 2026. arXiv:2603.15569
